          <declname>ret_handles</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Create new display panel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For maximum flexibility, this function performs only reset and initialization of the display. You must turn on the display explicitly by calling esp_lcd_panel_disp_on_off(). The display&apos;s backlight is not turned on either. You can use bsp_display_backlight_on/off(), <ref refid="group__g04__display_1ga12c7b53be5b337029f2d1aacce916d1c" kindref="member">bsp_display_brightness_set()</ref> (on supported boards) or implement your own backlight control.</para>
<para>If you want to free resources allocated by this function, you can use API:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="group__g04__display_1gae3c41ec26043f11aa620c6aa4dd2a36b" kindref="member">bsp_display_delete</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>display configuration </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">ret_handles</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>all esp_lcd handles in one structure </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>ESP_OK On success</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Other errors from underlying esp_lcd driver </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
